import{$ as e,Bt as t,Ct as n,E as r,Et as i,I as a,It as o,J as s,Lt as c,M as l,Mt as u,N as d,Q as f,Rt as p,S as m,T as ee,Tt as h,U as g,Vt as _,X as v,Y as y,_ as b,_t as x,dt as S,et as C,gt as w,ht as T,j as E,jt as D,ot as te,q as O,rt as k,ut as A,vt as j,wt as M,xt as N,yt as P,z as F,zt as ne}from"../chunks/C70YxWkr.js";import{a as I,c as L,d as R,i as z,l as re,n as ie,r as B,s as V,u as ae}from"../chunks/Yw925n3J.js";import{F as oe,I as H,M as se,P as ce,S as le,b as ue,d as U,l as de,m as fe,n as pe,v as me,y as he}from"../chunks/C6x6CAgf.js";import{C as ge,D as _e,E as ve,S as ye,_ as be,a as W,b as xe,d as Se,g as Ce,m as we,n as Te,o as Ee,p as De,t as Oe,v as ke,w as Ae,x as je,y as Me}from"../chunks/BLXeGs1u.js";import{t as Ne}from"../chunks/DlrcSjRK.js";import{t as Pe}from"../chunks/G_UieWOb.js";import{i as Fe,n as Ie,o as G,s as Le}from"../chunks/BNnLn8XG.js";import{t as Re}from"../chunks/JOxVDZdS.js";import{l as ze}from"../chunks/CtYVLT1i.js";import{a as Be,i as Ve,n as He,r as Ue,t as We}from"../chunks/DTIm75iq.js";import{t as Ge}from"../chunks/BMuIX737.js";import{i as Ke}from"../chunks/NMRsKvgP.js";import{n as qe,t as Je}from"../chunks/3eqlaB_y.js";var K={TIP:{thr:`The level above which the signal is squashed`,ratio:`How many times the excess is squashed`,att:`How fast the compressor squeezes`,rel:`How fast the compressor lets go`,knee:`How smooth the transition at the threshold is`,mk:`Brings the loudness back after compression`,clip:`Gently cuts the peaks above the ceiling`,mix:`Share of the compressed signal in the mix with the original`,sc:`The detector does not hear the low end below this frequency`,look:`The compressor reacts in advance`,gap:`The length of the silence between phrases`},STYLES:{clean:`Clean`,classic:`Classic`,opto:`Opto`,vocal:`Vocal`,mastering:`Mastering`,bus:`Bus`,punch:`Punch`,pumping:`Pumping`},fmtMs:{ms:` ms`},CTRL:{porog:`Threshold`,smes:`Mix`,uroven_vyshe_kotorogo_kompressor:`The level above which the compressor starts turning the loudness down. Everything that fits into the yellow zone is left untouched. Lower the threshold and more of the signal gets processed.`,szhatie:`compression`,vo_skolko_raz_szhimaetsya:`How many times the excess above the threshold is squashed. At 4 : 1 a signal that was 12 dB above the threshold ends up 3 dB above. Compare the height of the semi-transparent and the solid bars above the threshold line: their ratio is the ratio. At ∞ : 1 this is a limiter.`,ataka:`Attack`,za_eto_vremya_posle:`In this time after the threshold is crossed the reduction reaches 90% of its value. The orange bracket under the top strip shows the length of the attack. The brackets turn red if most sounds end before the compressor gathers even half of the needed reduction. While it lasts, the start of the hit passes almost unchanged: with a long attack the first solid bars line up with the semi-transparent ones.`,reliz:`Release`,za_eto_vremya_posle_2:`In this time after the signal goes below the threshold the reduction lets go by 90%. The blue bracket shows the length of the release. With a long release the quiet tail after the hit stays pressed down. With a very short one the gain jitters inside every period of the wave and distorts it.`,koleno:`Knee`,shirina_zony_vokrug_poroga:`The width of the zone around the threshold where compression kicks in gradually. 0 dB - a hard knee, a kink on the curve. With a soft knee the compressor starts working a little before the threshold, and the transition is less audible.`,kompensatsiya:`Makeup`,usilenie_posle_szhatiya_kompressor:`Gain after compression. The compressor made the loud places quieter, and makeup lifts the whole signal back up. As a result the quiet places become louder than they were: watch how the solid bars in the tail grow past the semi-transparent ones.`,potolok:`ceiling`,vykl:`off`,myagkiy_ogranichitel_posle_kompres:`A soft limiter after the compressor and the makeup. The signal below half the ceiling (6 dB down) is unchanged, above it bends smoothly and never goes over the ceiling. Unlike the compressor it works instantly, on the waveform itself, so it catches the peaks that slipped past the slow attack. The price - distortion: the flattened tops add harmonics. Pink shows what is cut, the dashed line marks the ceiling. Zoom the wave in to individual periods to see the flattened tops.`,parallelnaya_kompressiya_k_szhatom:`Parallel compression: the original signal is mixed into the compressed one. 100 % - only the compressed, 0 % - only the original. The technique is this: compress very hard (low threshold, high ratio, fast attack), add makeup and mix in 30–50 %. The loud places and the attacks stay almost as in the original, because there the compressed signal is much quieter and adds little. The quiet places and the tails come up, because there the compressed signal is louder than the original. The reduction curve shows only the compressed branch; for the result look at the wave and at the phrase labels.`,sc_filtr:`SC filter`,srez_niza:`low cut`,gts:` Hz`,filtr_stoit_tolko_v:`The filter sits only in the detector’s chain: the compressor measures the level from the signal without the low end, but compresses the full signal. Bass and kick carry the most energy and make the compressor fire on every hit, which pumps everything else. Cut 80–150 Hz for the detector and it stops reacting to the low end: the reduction on the low notes gets smaller, while the low end itself stays in the sound. The turquoise outline on the wave shows what the detector hears. Try it on drums and on bass.`,operezhenie:`Lookahead`,kompressor_zaglyadyvaet_v_signal:`The compressor peeks a few milliseconds ahead in the signal and starts turning down in advance. The reduction curve shifts left and has time for the very start of the hit. That is how limiters work.`},markKnobs:{nizkovat:`a bit low?`,avto:`auto`,mnogovato:`a bit much?`,zhestkoe:`hard`,tolko_dry:`dry only`,kompensatsiya:`makeup`,avto_gromkost:`level match`,feyder:`fader before the compressor`,sc_filtr:`SC filter`,operezhenie:`lookahead`,vklyucheno:`On: `,soft_clip:`soft clip`,koleno_kompensatsiya_mix_sc:`Knee, Mix, SC filter, lookahead, soft clip`},buildChips:{stsenariy:`Scenario…`},abSwitch:{sravnenie_a_b:`A/B comparison`,dva_nabora_nastroek_na:`Two sets of settings on one signal. The knobs change the active set, which is shown as the green wave and the coloured reduction curve. The second set is visible as a light outline on the wave and a dashed line on the curve. Switch with the buttons or the A and B keys: during playback the sound changes at once. For a fair comparison, even out the loudness in both sets.`},GAPC:{pauzy:`Gaps`,menyaet_dlinu_tishiny_mezhdu:`Changes the length of the silence between phrases in the signal itself; the phrases themselves stay as they are. ×1 - as recorded, ×0.5 - the gaps are twice as short, ×4 - four times longer. The gap does not get shorter than 30 ms, so that neighbouring phrases do not merge. It is there to show the link between the release and the gap: shorten the gaps until the compressor stops having time to let go, and watch the release remark under the graph and the “Min. gap” label. On a signal with no silence between the sounds, on dense drums for example, the knob changes almost nothing.`},syncGap:{v_signale:`in the signal`},FA:{btn:`File breakdown`,line_spread:(e,t)=>` · phrase spread ${e} dB, peaks ${t} dB above average`,line_flat:e=>` · no gaps, peaks ${e} dB above average`,v_spread:e=>`Phrases of different loudness: spread ${e} dB`,v_spread_x:e=>`Phrases: ${e}, the loudest noticeably louder than the quietest. Goal - half the spread: start with “Even out”.`,v_hits:`Drum material: short sounds with a sharp start`,v_hits_x:`The compressor works on the shape of the hit. “Bring out the hit” will pass the click and press the body, “Tame the peaks” will cut the click. The hits do not need to be evened out among themselves.`,v_peaks:e=>`The loudness is even, but the peaks are high: ${e} dB above average`,v_peaks_x:`The phrases barely need evening out. Here the compressor works on separate spikes: “Tame the peaks” will press them down, “Bring out the hit” will emphasize them instead.`,v_dense:`The material is already dense`,dense_sp:e=>`Phrase spread ${e} dB. `,v_dense_x:(e,t)=>`${e}The peaks are only ${t} dB above the average level. Compression will change little here; if you set it, go gentle and a couple of decibels.`,crest:e=>`Peaks ${e} dB above the average level`,crest_hi:`Short spikes much louder than the body. A fast attack at a high ratio will cut them, a slow one will pass them.`,crest_mid:`Moderate dynamics, the usual kind for vocals and live instruments. A ratio of 2–4 : 1 fits.`,crest_lo:`Almost no peaks: the signal is already compressed or naturally even. A high ratio is not needed.`,lt1:`under 1 ms`,tr_sharp:(e,t)=>`Sharp hits: rise ${e}, peak sticks out ${t} dB`,tr_sharp_x:`The fate of such a hit is decided by the attack: under 1 ms cuts the click, 15–40 ms passes it whole.`,tr_soft:e=>`Sounds start smoothly: rise around ${e}`,tr_soft_x:`There is nothing to cut here, so the attack is not critical: 10–30 ms keeps the start of the notes.`,tr_mid:e=>`Sounds of medium sharpness start: rise around ${e}`,tr_mid_x:`An attack of 5–15 ms keeps the consonants and the start of the notes; anything shorter makes the sound duller.`,gap:e=>`Shortest gap ${e} ms`,gap_x:`This is the ceiling for the release: if it is longer, the next phrase will start pressed down.`,ioi:e=>`No gaps, sounds come about every ${e} ms`,ioi_x:`The release is set by the rhythm: about half of this interval, so that the reduction gets back before the next hit.`,nogap:`No gaps, no distinct rhythm`,nogap_x:`There is nothing to go by: set the release by ear, start at 150 ms.`,low:e=>`Below 120 Hz - ${e} % of the energy`,low_mix_x:`The low end will make the compressor fire and pump everything else. An SC filter at around 100 Hz helps.`,low_bass_x:`This is a bass part: keep the release no shorter than 50 ms, or the compressor will start distorting the waveform.`,thr_quiet:`At the peak level of the quietest phrase: the compressor will not touch it, and will turn the loud ones down.`,thr_l50:`There are no separate phrases, so the level is taken at which the signal is above half the time.`,thr_l90:`Only the loudest 10 % of the material stays above the threshold.`,thr_body:`At the average level: the compressor squashes the body of the sound, not just the peaks.`,ratio_half:e=>`So that the loudest phrase drops by about ${e} dB - half of the spread.`,ratio_soft:`Gentle compression of a few decibels.`,ratio_tame:`Almost a limiter: the excess above the threshold is squashed eight times.`,ratio_punch:`Enough to bring the body of the sound noticeably down relative to the hit.`,att_pass:`The start of the sound passes, and the compressor takes the body.`,att_catch:`Faster than the hit rises: the compressor makes it to the peak.`,att_through:`Noticeably longer than the rise: the hit passes whole.`,rel_gap:`By the shortest gap.`,rel_ioi:`Half of the interval between hits.`,rel_def:`An average starting point: there are no gaps in the file.`,rel_fast:`Short, so that the compressor lets go between the peaks.`,rel_low:` Not shorter than 50 ms, because of the bass.`,knee_soft:`A soft transition, the compression is less noticeable.`,knee_hard:`Hard: a clear line between the hit and the body.`,sc:`The detector does not hear the low end and does not pump the rest.`,punch_nofit:`There are no distinct hits in the file, so there is nothing to bring out: this goal will change little here.`,applied_t:`Starting settings for the file`,applied_x:`The knobs are set from the file breakdown. Compare with the original through Bypass and fine-tune: the “What is happening” line under the graph will show what is not keeping up.`},on_file:{vzyaty_pervye_20_sekund:` - first 20 seconds taken`,ne_poluchilos_prochitat_fayl:`Could not read the file. Try a WAV or MP3.`},modeClick:{edinaya_shkala:`One scale`,vid_kak_v_fabfilter:`The view as in FabFilter Pro-C 2. The level is plotted from bottom to top in decibels: the light silhouette - input, the solid one - output. The reduction curve hangs from the top at the same scale, so its depth exactly equals the gap between input and output below it. On the right is the knee curve on the same vertical scale: the threshold on it and the threshold line on the wave sit at the same height.`},LABH:{gromkost_fraz:`Loudness of phrases`,signal_razbit_na_frazy:`The signal is split into phrases by the gaps. Every phrase is labeled with its average loudness before and after compression. The spread - the difference between the loudest and the quietest phrase. It hints at how much reduction is needed for evening out: if the compressor turns down more than the original spread, the phrases are already even and from there only the dynamics suffer. This is a landmark for vocals, bass and other parts made of separate phrases. When dense compression is the goal - on drums, or as an effect - going past the spread is fine, so the hint is grey rather than red.`,piki_fraz:`Peaks of phrases`,to_zhe_samoe_no:`The same thing, but by the highest peak of each phrase. The peaks show how high a phrase jumps above the threshold, the average loudness shows how much energy it carries.`,pauzy_mezhdu_frazami:`Gaps between phrases`,podpisana_dlina_kazhdoy_pauzy:`Every gap is labeled with its length. A gap turns red if by the start of the next phrase the compressor has not let go and the phrase starts pressed down. The shortest gap turns green when the release fits inside it. This is a landmark for the release: if it is longer than the gap, the compressor does not have time to let go and presses down the start of the next, quiet phrase. Set the release equal to the shortest gap and compare the loudness labels of the quiet phrases.`},on_labs:{eti_podpisi_stoyat_vnizu:` These labels stand at the bottom of the graph.`,eti_podpisi_stoyat_vverhu:` These labels stand at the top of the graph.`,pauzy_otmecheny_skobkami_na:` Gaps are marked with brackets on the middle line.`,vse_tri_sloya_mozhno:` All three layers can be on at once.`},STYH:{shema_s_obratnoy_svyazyu:`A feedback scheme, like in old hardware compressors: the detector listens not to the input but to the already compressed output. So the behaviour depends on the material: the further the signal goes above the threshold and the higher the ratio, the faster the attack fires. The release comes out smoother and more drawn out, because as it lets go the output climbs above the threshold again. The knee is hard, its knob does nothing.`,ratio_i_koleno_kompressor:`The compressor picks the ratio and the knee itself: a very wide soft knee of 18 dB and a moderate compression of 4 : 1. What is left to set is the threshold, the attack and the release. Quiet words are almost untouched, loud ones are pressed down smoothly, with no obvious point where it kicks in. The ratio and knee knobs are dimmed.`,prozrachnaya_osnovnaya_ogibayuscha:`A transparent main envelope with your attack and release, plus a separate fast peak catcher. It kicks in only when a spike needs 6 dB more reduction than the current one, fires in fractions of a millisecond and lets go in 30 ms. You can set a slow attack without fearing that a sharp peak will slip through whole. The knee is no harder than 6 dB.`,dlya_shiny_i_skleyki:`For the bus and “glue”. The detector averages the level over 30 ms and does not react to separate short peaks, so the reduction curve is smooth and shared by the whole mix. The release is double: fast after short events and a slow tail after long compression. The knee is no harder than 6 dB.`,narochitoe_kachanie_posle_udara:`Deliberate “pumping”. After the hit the reduction is held for 30 ms, then comes back in a straight line in decibels over the release time. On the curve that is a steady slope instead of a fading exponential, and by ear - the characteristic rising “breath” between the hits. It shows up best on drums with a deep threshold and a high ratio.`,obychnaya_model_posle_prevysheniya:`An ordinary model: after the threshold is crossed the reduction goes smoothly, exponentially, toward its target and lets go just as smoothly. The attack and release times mean exactly what they say: 90% of the way in that time.`,ataka_nabiraetsya_s_obrazno:`The attack gathers in an S-shape: for the first milliseconds the compressor barely presses, then it squeezes harder than usual and reaches 90% in the same time. The start of the hit passes more intact than in Clean at the same attack, and the body of the sound is pressed down just as much. Compare the left slope of the dips on the reduction curve: in Clean it is steep right away, here it starts out gentle.`,kak_u_opticheskih_kompressorov:`Like in optical compressors: the knee is always soft (never harder than 12 dB), and the release depends on the material. After a short peak the reduction lets go quickly, about three times faster than the set release. After a long loud phrase it lets go quickly only for the first third and holds the rest for a long time. On the curve that shows as a kink on the right slope. The release bracket here shows only the nominal time.`},on_style:{stil:`Style `,eto_uproschennye_modeli_po:` These are simplified models along a common principle, not the algorithms of FabFilter.`},on_dets:{detektor:`Detector`,pikovyy_detektor_reagiruet_na:`The peak detector catches every spike. RMS averages over 10 ms and fires later, more gently.`},on_ride:{feyder:`Fader before the compressor`,pervaya_stupen:`The first stage before the compressor: the loudness of every phrase is pulled to the average by 70% of the difference, the way you would do it by hand with a fader, automation or clip gain. A phrase moves as a whole, so its shape and the dynamics inside it do not change. The grey wave - the signal already after this stage, and it is what Bypass plays. The compressor is left to remove a small remainder of the spread. On a signal with no separate phrases the button changes nothing.`},on_match:{avto_gromkost:`Level match`,szhatyy_signal_tishe_ishodnogo:`The compressed signal is quieter than the original, and after makeup it can become louder. The ear takes “louder” for “better”, so “before” and “after” can only be compared honestly at equal loudness. While the mode is on, makeup is matched by itself after every turn of any knob, so that the average level (RMS) at the output equals the input. The makeup knob shows the matched value; turning it by hand switches the mode off. Makeup does not drop below zero: if the output is already louder than the input, it stays louder.`},MINGAP_T:{pauza_mezhdu_frazami_edinstvennoe:`The gap between phrases - the only time when the compressor can bring the loudness back. If the release is longer than the gap, by the start of the next phrase the reduction is still not off, and the phrase sounds quieter than it should.`,silnee_vsego_stradayut_tihie:`Quiet phrases after loud ones suffer the most: you set a compressor so that they become audible, and it presses them down even further.`,orientirovatsya_stoit_na_samuyu:`Aim by the shortest gap, not the average: if the release fits inside it, it will fit inside all the rest too.`,eto_potolok_a_ne:`This is a ceiling, not a required value. The release can be set shorter, but too short a one starts distorting the low frequencies, so usually a value a little under the shortest gap is taken.`,proverit_na_glaz_pomogaet:`The “Gaps” knob helps you check by eye: squeeze the gaps and watch from which moment the release remark under the graph turns red.`},on_phr:{pochemu_vazhna_minimalnaya_pauza:`Why the shortest gap matters`},EX:{"att-pass":{n:`The start of the hit passes`,q:`Why does the start of the hit pass with almost no reduction?`,opts:[`The threshold is too high`,`The attack is longer than the hit itself`,`The release is too short`,`The ratio is too low`],ok:`The reduction takes 40 ms to build up, while the peak of the hit lasts a few milliseconds: the compressor arrives when the hit has already passed. On the reduction curve that is the left slope of the dip.`,wrong:{0:`The threshold is low enough here: the compressor squeezes the body of the hit, so the signal does reach it.`,2:`The release controls how the reduction goes away, - that is the right slope of the dip. It does not affect the start of the hit.`,3:`The ratio sets the depth of the dip, not the moment it begins.`},try:`Set attack to 0.3 ms`,marks:{ask:[`The start of the hit: “after” matches “before”`],done:[`The left slope - attack: the reduction is still building up, and the peak has already passed`]},optMarks:{2:`The right slope - release, your answer`}},"rel-carry":{n:`Phrases after gaps are quieter`,q:`Why do phrases after gaps start quieter than they should?`,opts:[`The attack is too fast`,`The release is longer than the gap between phrases`,`The threshold is too low`,`There is not enough makeup`],ok:`The gap - that is the only time the compressor has to bring the loudness back. A release of 400 ms is longer than the gap, so the next phrase starts already pressed down.`,wrong:{0:`A fast attack cuts the start of the sound, but only when the signal is already above the threshold. Here the phrase is pressed down before it even begins.`,2:`A low threshold increases the depth of the reduction, but does not stop it from running past the gap.`,3:`Makeup lifts everything the same way and does not change the difference between the phrases.`},try:`Set the release by the shortest gap`,marks:{ask:[`The gap has ended, and the reduction has not gone away yet`],done:[`Release: the reduction takes longer to go away than the gap lasts`]},optMarks:{0:`The left slope - attack, your answer`}},"thr-quiet":{n:`The quiet phrase did not change`,q:`Why did the loud phrases become quieter, while the quietest one did not change?`,opts:[`The attack does not keep up on the quiet phrase`,`The quiet phrase does not rise above the threshold`,`The ratio acts only on loud sounds`,`The release holds the reduction on the quiet phrase`],ok:`The compressor touches only what is above the threshold. The threshold stands at the peak level of the quietest phrase, so it passes unchanged while the loud ones are turned down.`,wrong:{0:`The attack matters only when the signal is already above the threshold.`,2:`The ratio is the same for everything above the threshold. The question is what ended up above it.`,3:`Then the quiet phrase would have become quieter, but it did not change.`},try:`Lower the threshold by 8 dB`,marks:{ask:[`This phrase is the same before and after`],done:[`The peaks of this phrase are not above the threshold: the compressor leaves it alone`]}},"ratio-ab":{n:`Compare two versions`,q:`Which version has the higher ratio?`,opts:[`A - the green wave`,`B - the light contour`,`They are the same`],ok:`B has deeper dips on the reduction curve at the same threshold: the same excess above it is squashed harder. The threshold, attack and release are the same in both.`,wrong:{0:`A has shallower dips: the same excess above the threshold is squashed less.`,2:`Compare the depth of the dips on the reduction curve: the dashed one is deeper.`}},"rel-predict":{n:`What a long release does`,q:`What changes if the release goes from 60 to 600 ms?`,opts:[`The start of every hit will pass for longer`,`The reduction will not have time to go away before the next hit`,`The dips will start before the hit`],ok:`The release - that is the time the reduction takes to go away. At 600 ms it has no time to come back to zero between the hits, and the next hit starts already pressed down. That is how “pumping” appears.`,wrong:{0:`The start of the hit depends on the attack; the release does not affect it.`,2:`The compressor acts before the hit only with lookahead.`},try:`Set release to 600 ms`,marks:{done:[`The right slope: the reduction takes longer to go away than the interval between the hits`]}},"two-stage":{n:`Even, but crushed`,q:`The phrases became even, but the loud one is pressed down by more than 20 dB and sounds flat. How do you get the same evenness more gently?`,opts:[`Raise the ratio so the compressor presses harder`,`Lengthen the attack`,`Even out the phrases by loudness by hand first and leave the compressor 2–3 dB`,`Add makeup`],ok:`The spread of the phrases here is almost 10 dB, and one compressor removes it only with deep compression: together with the difference between phrases it also flattens the dynamics inside each one. A fader moves the phrase as a whole and does not touch its shape. When the phrases are already pulled together by hand, the compressor needs only 2–3 dB: the spread at the output is the same, and the reduction is several times smaller.`,wrong:{0:`The ratio is already 8 : 1. Any higher - that is almost a limiter: the phrases will level out, but flatten even more.`,1:`A long attack will let the start of the notes through, but the body of every note will stay pressed down just as deep.`,3:`Makeup lifts everything the same way: the depth of compression and the flat sound remain.`},try:`Even out the phrases by hand and leave the compressor 3 dB`,marks:{ask:[`The loud phrase: reduction over 20 dB`],done:[`The same phrase: compare the depth of reduction before and after the button`]}},"att-match":{n:`Match the attack to the contour`,q:`Set the attack so that the start of the hit passes as on the contour`,hint:`Watch the first milliseconds of the hit. Where the green wave is above the light contour, the compressor is later than the goal; where it is below - it arrives earlier. The “Goal” button plays the answer.`,ok:`The shorter the attack, the smaller part of the hit passes without reduction. The threshold, ratio and release were not changed here.`},guess:{n:`Guess the settings`,q:`Set the threshold, ratio, attack and release so that the wave matches the contour`,hint:`Start with the threshold: lower it until the depth of the dips on the reduction curve looks like the dashed line. Then the ratio: it changes the depth of all the dips at once. Set the attack by the left slope of each dip, the release - by the right one. The “Goal” button plays the answer.`,ok:`Different combinations of threshold and ratio can give almost the same picture, so a small mismatch of values is not a mistake.`,score:e=>`Match of the reduction curves: ${e} %.`}},tips:{gr_title:`How hard the compressor presses the sound at each moment. The lower the line, the harder.`,gr_scale:`Reduction in decibels - how much the compressor turned the level down.`,gr_val:`How hard the compressor pressed this phrase, dB.`,rel:`Release - how fast the compressor lets go of the sound after a loud spot.`,att:`Attack - how fast the compressor grabs the sound once it gets louder than the threshold.`,gap:`Pauses between phrases. Release should not be longer than the shortest one.`,loud:`Loudness of the phrase before and after the compressor, dB. The closer the numbers across phrases, the more even the sound.`,peak:`The loudest instant of the phrase before and after the compressor, dB.`,level:`Signal level in dB. 0 is the loudest, lower is quieter.`,thr:`Threshold - above this line the compressor starts pressing the sound.`,before:`The sound before the compressor.`,after:`The sound after the compressor.`,time:`Time from the start of the recording.`},drawBody:{podavlenie_sverhu_v_tom:`Reduction on top, at the same scale`,podavlenie_db:`Reduction, dB`,bypass_obrabotka_vyklyuchena:` - Bypass, processing off`,ne_slyshno_mix_0:` - inaudible, Mix 0 %`,reliz:`release `,ataka:`attack `,t_do:`Before`,posle:`After`,ms:` ms`,pik:`peak `,porog:`threshold `,s:` s`},updateReadout:{t_ms_vhod_podavlenie:(e,t,n,r)=>`t = <b>${e} ms</b> · input <b>${t}</b> · reduction <b>${n}</b> · output <b>${r}</b>`},drawStats:{pik_do_posle:`Peak, before → after`,sredniy_uroven_rms:`Average level (RMS)`,pik_minus_rms:`Crest factor`,maks_podavlenie:`Max. reduction`,kompressor_v_rabote:`Compressor at work`,vremeni:` % of the time`,peregruz:`Overload`,vyhod_vyshe_0_db:`output above 0 dB`},drawPhr:{otdelnyh_fraz_net:`No separate phrases`,gromkaya:(e,t)=>`Loud<b>${e} → ${t}</b>`,tihaya:(e,t)=>`Quiet<b>${e} → ${t}</b>`,razbros_db:(e,t)=>`Spread<b>${e} → ${t} dB</b>`,razbros_pikov_db:(e,t)=>`Peak spread<b>${e} → ${t} dB</b>`,maks_pik:(e,t)=>`Max. peak<b>${e} → ${t}</b>`,min_pik:(e,t)=>`Min. peak<b>${e} → ${t}</b>`,potolok_dlya_reliza_esli:`The ceiling for the release: if the release is longer, the next phrase will start pressed down. Click to read more`,min_pauza_ms:e=>`Min. gap<b>${e} ms</b>`,reliz_ms:e=>`Release = ${e} ms`},drawDiag:{mix_0_na_vyhod:`Mix 0 %: only the original signal goes to the output`,porog_ratio_ataka_reliz:`Threshold, ratio, attack, release, knee, makeup, lookahead and the SC filter do not affect anything right now, so their knobs are dimmed. Only soft clip works - it sits after the mixing.`,krivaya_podavleniya_pokazyvaet_cht:`The reduction curve shows what the compressed branch would do.`,podnimite_mix_chtoby_uslyshat:`Raise Mix to hear the compressor`,ne_rabotaet:`Not working`,kompressor_pochti_ne_rabotaet:`The compressor barely works`,signal_ne_podnimaetsya_nad:`The signal does not rise above the threshold by any number of decibels.`,opustite_porog_poka_na:`Lower the threshold until dips appear on the reduction curve.`,opustite_porog:`Lower the threshold`,ataka_reshaet_sohranitsya_li:`The attack decides whether the start of the sound survives: the consonants of a voice, the click of the drums.`,ataka_s_pervyh_ms:`Attack from the first ms`,ataka_nachalo_zvuka_srezano:`Attack: the start of the sound is cut`,kompressor_srabatyvaet_s_pervyh:`The compressor fires from the first milliseconds of the phrase. The peaks are under control.`,uvelichivayte_ataku_esli_zvuk:` Raise the attack if the sound has gone dull.`,ataka:(e,t)=>`Attack ${e}/${t}`,ataka_opazdyvaet:`The attack is late`,na_iz_uchastkov_nad:(e,t)=>`On ${e} of ${t} sections above the threshold the sound ends before the compressor gathers half of the needed reduction. Such brackets are red.`,ataka_dlinnee_bolshinstva_zvukov:e=>`The attack of ${e} is longer than most sounds. Shorten it or lower the threshold.`,priem_nachnite_s_samoy:`Technique: start with the fastest attack and raise it`,ataka_ms:e=>`Attack ${e} ms`,ataka_nachalo_zvuka_prohodit:`Attack: the start of the sound passes`,pervye_ms_kazhdoy_frazy:e=>`The first ~${e} ms of every phrase pass with almost no reduction.`,esli_reliz_ne_uspevaet:`If the release does not keep up, quiet phrases after loud ones become even quieter. That is the opposite of what a compressor is set for.`,reliz:(e,t)=>`Release ${e}/${t}`,reliz_ne_uspevaet_otpustit:`The release does not keep up letting go`,iz_fraz_nachinayutsya_uzhe:(e,t,n,r)=>`${e} of ${t} phrases already start pressed down, down to −${n} dB. The release is now ${r}.`,samaya_korotkaya_pauza_ms:e=>` The shortest gap is ${e} ms: the release should fit inside it, and then it will fit inside all the rest too.`,priem_reliz_po_samoy:e=>`Technique: release by the shortest gap, ${e} ms`,reliz_uspevaet:`The release keeps up`,reliz_uspevaet_otpustit:`The release keeps up letting go`,k_nachalu_kazhdoy_sleduyuschey:`By the start of every next phrase the reduction is back almost to zero.`,iskazheniya:`Distortion`,reliz_slishkom_bystryy:`The release is too fast`,podavlenie_drozhit_na_db:e=>`The reduction jitters by ${e} dB inside a single wave. That is distortion, not compression.`,derzhite_reliz_dlinnee_pary:`Keep the release longer than a couple of periods of the lowest note, from 40–50 ms on bass.`,priem_reliz_ne_koroche:`Technique: release not shorter than the period of the bass`,mix_podmeshan_ishodnyy_signal:e=>`Mix ${e} %: the original signal is mixed in`,na_samom_gromkom_meste:(e,t)=>`At the loudest place the level really drops by ${e} dB, not by ${t} dB.`,krivaya_podavleniya_pokazyvaet_tol:`The reduction curve shows only the compressed branch; for the result look at the wave and at the phrase labels.`,sc_gts:e=>`SC ${e} Hz`,sc_filtr_gts:e=>`SC filter ${e} Hz`,detektor_ne_slyshit_niz:`The detector does not hear the low end and reacts only to what is above it.`,biryuzovyy_kontur_na_volne:`The turquoise outline on the wave shows its signal.`,orientir:`Landmark`,orientir_ne_oshibka_podavlenie:`A landmark, not a mistake: the reduction is bigger than the spread`,podavlenie_db_bolshe_razbrosa:(e,t)=>`The reduction is ${e} dB bigger than the spread of the phrases (${t} dB).`,porog_nizhe_samoy_tihoy:`the threshold is below the quietest phrase, try raising it`,poprobuyte_umenshit_ratio:`try lowering the ratio`,dlya_vyravnivaniya_gromkosti_eto:e=>`To even out the loudness this is too much: ${e}. For a deliberately dense compression it is fine.`,porog_nizhe_samoy_tihoy_2:`The threshold is below the quietest phrase`,ratio_bolshe_chem_nuzhno:`The ratio is higher than evening out needs`,feyder:`Fader`,frazy_podtyanuty_vruchnuyu:`The phrases were pulled together by hand before the compressor`,razbros_na_vhode:(e,t)=>`The spread of phrase loudness at the compressor’s input: it was ${e} dB, now it is ${t} dB.`,gromkost_kazhdoy_frazy_sdvinuta:`Every phrase is shifted in loudness as a whole, so its shape and dynamics do not change. The grey wave and Bypass show the signal already after this stage. The compressor is left with 2–3 dB to remove.`,clip_ne_dostaet:`Clip does not reach`,soft_clip_vklyuchen_no:`Soft clip is on but does not work`,signal_ne_dohodit_do:`The signal does not reach half the ceiling.`,opustite_potolok_ili_dobavte:`Lower the ceiling or add makeup.`,clip_db:e=>`Clip −${e} dB`,soft_clip_srezaet_piki:`Soft clip is cutting the peaks`,s_pikov_uhodit_do:(e,t)=>`Up to ${e} dB comes off the peaks, the clipper works ${t} % of the time.`,eto_uzhe_slyshimye_iskazheniya:`These are already audible distortions: raise the ceiling or let the compressor remove more.`,rozovym_na_volne_pokazano:`Pink on the wave shows what is cut.`,podnimite_potolok_soft_clip:`Raise the soft clip ceiling`,peregruz:`Overload`,peregruz_vyhod_vyshe_0:`Overload: output above 0 dB`,pik_na_vyhode:e=>`Peak at the output ${e}.`,ubavte_kompensatsiyu_ili_vklyuchit:`Turn makeup down or switch on soft clip.`,ubavte_kompensatsiyu:`Turn makeup down`},drawAB:{podavlenie_do_db:(e,t)=>`<b>${e}</b>: reduction up to −${t} dB`,razbros_db:e=>`, spread ${e} dB`,kontur:` (contour)`},html:{see_bus:`Bus glue`,name:`Compressor`,start:`Here you can see and hear what a compressor does to loudness and what every knob of it changes.`,start_1:`Press Play and listen to the example.`,start_2:`Turn one knob - “Threshold”. The graph and the sound change at once.`,slushat_ishodnyy_signal_bez:`Listen to the source signal, unprocessed`,slushat_zagadannyy_rezultat:`Listen to the target`,vid:`View`,nalozhenie_do_i_posle:`Overlay: before and after on one wave`,edinaya_shkala_uroven_snizu:`Level at the bottom, reduction on top, knee curve on the right`,razrez_polovina_volny_ot:`Cut: half a wave from zero up`,do_i_posle_na:`Before and after on two tracks`,vid_overlay:`Overlay`,vid_proc:`Single scale`,vid_cut:`Cut`,vid_split:`Two lanes`,detektor:`Detector`,pikovyy_detektor_reagiruet_na:`Peak detector: reacts to every spike`,rms_detektor_usrednyaet_uroven:`RMS detector: averages the level over 10 ms`,signal:`Signal`,esche_vidy_stsenarii_igra:`More: views and scenarios`,stsenariy:`Scenario`,podpisi_fraz:`Phrase labels`,volna_do_i_posle:`Waveform before and after compression, reduction curve`,stil_kompressii:`Compressor style`,kompensatsiya_podbiraetsya_sama_ch:`Makeup is matched by itself so that the average loudness before and after is the same. That way Bypass and A/B compare dynamics, not loudness`,zachem_eto_prilozhenie:`What this app is for`,tsel:`Goal`,pik:`Peak`,vokal_penie:`Vocal: singing`,vokal_rep:`Vocal: rap`,udarnye:`Drums`,test_ton:`Test tone`,bas:`Bass`,svoy_fayl:`Your own file (first 20 s)…`,shkala:`Scale`,lineynaya_shkala_amplitudy:`Linear amplitude scale`,nastroyki:`Settings`,podpisi:`Labels`,gromkost:`Loudness`,piki:`Peaks`,pauzy:`Gaps`,myagkiy_klip:`Soft clip`,koleso_priblizhaet_peretaskivanie:`The wheel or a pinch zooms, dragging moves, and the threshold line can be dragged. Views, detector, style and labels are in the “…” menu.`,t_do:`before`,posle:`after`,porog:`threshold`,ataka:`attack`,reliz:`release`,detektor_2:`detector`,avto_gromkost:`Level match`,feyder:`Fader before the compressor`,pervaya_stupen_gromkost_kazhdoy:`First stage: the loudness of every phrase is already pulled to the average by hand, so the compressor has less work left`,klyuch_tsvetov:`To understand what a compressor does with your eyes. In plugins its action is usually shown as a diagram or a conditional graph, and it is hard to tie turning a knob to what happens to the sound. Here you see the real waveform before and after processing, and every knob move changes the picture at once.`,kak_polzovatsya:`How to use the cheat sheet`,vyberite_signal_penie_rep:`Pick a signal: singing, rap, drums, test tone, bass, or your own file. From a file the first 20 seconds are taken; after the load, its breakdown with starting settings appears in the Inspector.`,povernite_odnu_ruchku_i:`Turn one knob and watch how the green wave changes against the grey one.`,sledite_za_indikatorami_pod:`Watch the “What is happening” line under the graph: a red dot means the compressor is not keeping up with something. Clicking a remark opens an explanation: what exactly, and what to turn.`,modeli_uproscheny:`The “Techniques” section in the Inspector shows on examples how to pick attack, release and threshold. Matching settings to the contour (“guess the settings”) - the last task of the trainer. The compressor models here are simplified: the character of the behaviour is the same, but the numbers may not match your plugin.`,chto_seychas_proishodit:`What is happening now`,parametr:`Parameter`,kak_chitat_kartinku:`How to read the picture`,vse_chto_vyshe_fioletovoy:`Everything above the violet threshold line the compressor turns down. The top strip shows by how many decibels it turned the loudness down at each moment. The orange parts of the curve - the compressor is squeezing (attack), the blue ones - it lets go (release). Red marks only what does not have time to act.`,priemy:`Techniques`,fa_title:`File breakdown`,fa_start:`Where to start`,fa_goal:`Goal of the compression`,fa_even:`Even out`,fa_tame:`Tame the peaks`,fa_punch:`Bring out the hit`,fa_apply:`Apply these settings`,fa_note:`This is a starting point, calculated from the first 20 seconds of the file, not a ready answer. Fine-tune it by ear and by the “What is happening” line under the graph.`},GOAL:{start:(e,t)=>`Loudness jumps by ${e} dB. The task: ${t} dB or less.`,run:(e,t)=>`Loudness spread is ${e} dB. The task: ${t} dB or less.`,intro:`A ready-made example setting to start with. Press Play, switch Bypass on and off and hear the difference. The graph marks what the compressor did.`,mark_loud:`Loud part: gray before, green after`,mark_quiet:`Quiet part: almost untouched`,mark_gap:`Pause: the compressor lets go`,done:(e,t)=>`Loudness spread was ${e} dB, now ${t}: goal reached.`},SCEN:{po_razbrosu_i_pauze:`By spread and gap`,porog_stoit_na_urovne:`The threshold sits at the peaks of the quietest phrase: the compressor leaves it alone and turns the loud ones down. The release equals the shortest gap. Adjust the ratio until the spread shrinks to about half.`,myagko_vyrovnyat:`Even out gently`,nevysokoe_ratio_i_myagkoe:`A moderate ratio and a soft knee. The peaks drop by a few decibels, the shape of the hits barely changes.`,propustit_udar:`Let the hit through`,ataka_40_ms_nachalo:`Attack 40 ms. The start of the hit passes whole, and the compressor squeezes the body of the sound instead. The hit becomes clicky and dense. Compare the first bars: before and after they are the same.`,pridavit_udar:`Press the hit down`,ataka_0_3_ms:`Attack 0.3 ms. The compressor gets to the very start and cuts the peak. The hit loses its edge, but it stops jumping out of the mix.`,limiter:`Limiter`,ratio_1_mgnovennaya_ataka:`Ratio ∞ : 1, instant attack and 2 ms of lookahead. Nothing gets above the threshold: every solid bar stops against the threshold line.`,shina_udarnyh:`Drums bus`,myagkaya_skleyka_vsey_ustanovki:`A gentle glue for the whole kit: the Bus style, ratio 2 : 1, attack 30 ms, reduction 1–3 dB. An attack of 20–40 ms lets the click of the kick and snare through, and the compressor presses only the bodies of the hits a little, so the kit plays like one instrument. If the reduction is deeper than 3–4 dB, the hits start to sag and between them the pumping is audible: raise the threshold.`,kachaet:`Pumping`,glubokoe_szhatie_i_dlinnyy:`Deep compression and a long release. After every hit the loudness comes back slowly, and the bed between the hits dips and swells by turns. That is the “pump”.`,iskazheniya:`Distortion`,reliz_2_ms_na:`Release 2 ms on the bass. The gain has time to change inside a single period of the wave, and the sine wave flattens. By ear that is rasp. Increase the release and the waveform comes back.`},TRICKS:{porog_po_samoy_tihoy:`Threshold by the quietest phrase, depth by the spread`,vklyuchite_podpisi_gromkosti_i:`Turn on the loudness labels and set the threshold just above the peaks of the quiet phrase. Reduction - no deeper than half the spread.`,reliz_po_samoy_korotkoy:`Release by the shortest gap`,pauza_mezhdu_frazami_eto:`The gap between phrases - that is all the time the compressor has to let go. If the release is longer than the gap, the next phrase starts already pressed down, and the quiet words become even quieter. That is the opposite of what you need. In the example the release is 400 ms: count how many phrases start under reduction. Then press the button above the wave and compare. A check by eye: the blue bracket under the reduction strip must end before the start of the next phrase.`,ataka_ot_samoy_bystroy:`Attack: from the fastest to the slowest`,postavte_ataku_na_minimum:`Set the attack to the minimum: the compressor cuts the very start of the sound, and the hit or the consonant disappears. Now raise the attack slowly and watch the first milliseconds. As soon as the green wave catches up with the grey one at the start of the hit, the transient has passed whole. There is no point raising it further: the compressor will start arriving late for the body of the sound too. Landmarks: 0.1–3 ms cut the click; 10–30 ms keep the attack of the drums and the consonants of the voice; above 50 ms the compressor only has time to act on long notes.`,dve_stupeni_vmesto_odnoy:`Two stages instead of one: first the fader, then the compressor`,kogda_frazy_silno_raznye:`When the phrases differ a lot in loudness, one compressor evens them out only with deep compression - by 10–20 dB - and the sound turns flat. Split the work. First bring the phrases together by loudness: with a fader, automation or clip gain. A phrase moves as a whole, its shape does not change. Then set the compressor to 2–3 dB: it will smooth what is left. In the example “Fader before the compressor” is on in the advanced settings: switch it off and lower the threshold until the spread at the output is the same, - and compare the depth of the reduction.`,snachala_preuvelichte_potom_vernit:`Exaggerate first, then bring it back`,ataku_i_reliz_trudno:`Attack and release are hard to see under gentle compression. Lower the threshold and set ratio 20 : 1 so the reduction reaches 10–15 dB. In that state every move of the attack and release knobs is visible on the curve and audible. Dial in the times, then return the ratio to 2–4 : 1 and raise the threshold to the depth you need. After that the times do not need to change.`,reliz_v_temp:`Release in tempo`,na_ritmichnom_materiale_krivaya:`On rhythmic material the reduction curve must return to zero right before the next hit. Too short a release gives a jerky loudness between the hits. Too long a release does not have time to let go and eats the next hit. The starting point - the length of a beat: 60 000 divided by the tempo; for eighths - half of that. In the example 100 beats per minute, and an eighth lasts 300 ms. Start at 150–250 ms and watch that the blue rise of the curve ends by the start of the next hit.`,reliz_ne_koroche_perioda:`Release not shorter than the period of the bass`,period_noty_50_gts:`One period of a 50 Hz note lasts 20 ms. If the release is shorter than a couple of periods, the compressor has time to let go and squeeze again inside a single wave. On the picture the sine wave flattens, and by ear that is rasp. On bass and kick hold the release at 40–50 ms. With an attack shorter than 1–2 ms it is the same story. In the example the release is 2 ms: raise it until the green wave becomes smooth again.`,parallelnaya_kompressiya_szhat_zhe:`Parallel compression: squash hard and mix some back`,obychnoe_szhatie_opuskaet_gromkoe:`Ordinary compression turns the loud down. Parallel compression lifts the quiet and barely touches the loud. In the example the compressed branch is crushed and lifted by makeup, but mixed in at 40 %. Compare the labels: the loud hits changed little, the quiet parts and the tails became noticeably louder. Turn Mix to 100 % to see what it would be like without the original signal, then back.`,filtr_v_detektore_protiv:`A filter in the detector against pumping from the bass`,bochka_samaya_gromkaya_v:`The kick is the loudest thing in the mix, and the compressor on the bus ducks on every one of its hits, dragging everything else down with it. The SC filter removes the low end only from the detector’s signal. In the example the cut sits at 150 Hz. Turn the SC filter to “off” and back: compare the depth of the dips on the kick and on the snare. The higher the cut, the less the compressor reacts to the kick.`,penie_medlennee_i_myagche:`Singing: slower and softer`,u_peniya_dlinnye_noty:`Singing has long notes, a smooth start and a wide spread of loudness between quiet and loud places. Here the compressor evens out whole phrases rather than catching separate peaks. A starting point: ratio 2–4 : 1, soft knee, attack 10–30 ms, release 150–300 ms. In the example the Vocal style is on: it picks the ratio and the knee itself. The gaps are long, so the release can be set noticeably longer than on speech. Too fast a release is heard as a “breathing” of loudness inside a single note: shorten it to 20–30 ms and watch the reduction curve start to follow every swing of the note. The numbers here - starting points, not rules.`,rep_bystro_i_plotno:`Rap: fast and dense`,u_chitki_korotkie_slogi:`Rap has short syllables, sharp consonants and very short gaps, and a smaller spread of loudness than singing. The task is different: hold the voice at one level so that every word cuts through the dense beat. A starting point: ratio 4–8 : 1, attack 1–5 ms, release 30–80 ms. The release runs up against the smallest gap: in the example it equals it. If the attack is too fast, the consonants lose their click and the words sound limp: raise it until the start of the syllables comes back. Then switch the signal to “Vocal: singing” with the same knobs and compare the “What is happening” line and the spread: the same settings behave differently. The synthesized signals carry only rhythm and dynamics; to hear the real difference, load two of your own fragments through “Your own file”. The numbers here - starting points, not rules.`,sravnivayte_na_ravnoy_gromkosti:`Compare at equal loudness`,szhatyy_signal_tishe_posle:`The compressed signal is quieter, after makeup it is louder, and the ear takes “louder” for “better”. Before comparing through Bypass or A/B, turn on “Level match” in the advanced settings. Then you hear only the change in dynamics.`},buildTricks:{rekomendatsiy:` recommendations`,pokazat_na_volne:`Show on the wave`}},Ye=e=>e.leng